<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nalerigu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nalerigu is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, capital of the North East Region and the seat of the Nayiri, paramount chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamprusi">Mamprusi</a>. The Mamprugu court moved there from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gambaga">Gambaga</a> around 1700 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/na-atabia">Na Atabia</a>. Parts of an old defensive wall attributed to an earlier ruler, Na Jeringa, still survive around the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nalerigu.jpg" alt="Nalerigu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shahadusadik · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_old_church_at_Nalerigu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
